# /sdd-assumptions

Purpose:
  Track, validate, and manage project assumptions. Makes the assumption
  registry actionable by surfacing stale assumptions, unmapped assumptions,
  and assumption-to-decision linkages.

Owns: commands/sdd-assumptions.sdd

Description:
  Reads .sdd/assumptions/INDEX.sdd and linked project assumptions to
  produce an assumption health report. Identifies assumptions without
  validation evidence, assumptions not mapped to decisions or tasks,
  and assumptions older than the project threshold.

Usage:
  /sdd-assumptions
  /sdd-assumptions --stale
  /sdd-assumptions --unmapped
  /sdd-assumptions --validate
  /sdd-assumptions --json

Options:
  --stale      Show only assumptions past validation threshold
  --unmapped   Show assumptions not linked to decisions or tasks
  --validate   Run validation checks against current project state
  --json       Output machine-readable JSON

Mode: READ_ONLY (--validate is SUPERVISED)

Output:
  ASSUMPTIONS

    Total:        <count>
    Validated:    <count>
    Stale:        <count>
    Unmapped:     <count>
    At Risk:      <count>

  Assumption List:
    [ASM-001] status: validated | last_checked: <date> | linked: DEC-102, TASK-204
    [ASM-002] status: stale | last_checked: <date> | linked: none
    [ASM-003] status: at_risk | last_checked: <date> | linked: DEC-105

Rules:
  [ASM-01] /sdd-assumptions MUST NOT modify any file unless --validate is supplied.
  [ASM-02] Stale assumptions MUST be flagged for human review.
  [ASM-03] Unmapped assumptions MUST be linked to decisions or tasks or retired.
  [ASM-04] Assumption status MUST be derived from evidence_count and last_checked date.
  [ASM-05] --validate mode MUST require human approval before marking assumptions invalid.

Navigation:
   INDEX: @INDEX.sdd
   Assumptions: @../assumptions/INDEX.sdd
   Decisions: @../decisions/INDEX.sdd
   Tasks: @../tasks/INDEX.sdd
   Projects: @../projects/INDEX.sdd

State: +
